{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-72362","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-103543","text":"Competitive Landscape: Agent Governance and Runtime Enforcement"}]},{"id":"blk-72363","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103544","marks":["bold"],"text":"March 2026 -- OpenSentience"}]},{"id":"blk-72364","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-103545","text":"The field"}]},{"id":"blk-72365","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103546","text":"The AI agent market is projected at $48B by 2030 (BCC Research, 43.3% CAGR). Hundreds of companies are building agents. Almost none of them are building the governance layer that makes agents safe to deploy — and the few that attempt governance have made architectural commitments that prevent them from doing it correctly."}]},{"id":"blk-72366","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103547","text":"This document maps the competitive landscape by structural category, identifies the architectural constraints each category faces, and explains why those constraints compound over time as AI commoditizes implementation."}]},{"id":"blk-72367","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-103548","text":"Category 1: Orchestration frameworks without governance"}]},{"id":"blk-72368","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103549","marks":["bold"],"text":"Competitors:"},{"id":"spn-103550","text":" CrewAI, LangGraph/LangChain, AutoGen + Semantic Kernel (Microsoft)"}]},{"id":"blk-72369","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103551","text":"These frameworks wire agents together. None of them answer "},{"id":"spn-103552","marks":["italic"],"text":"who gets to decide what"},{"id":"spn-103553","text":", "},{"id":"spn-103554","marks":["italic"],"text":"what permissions does this agent have"},{"id":"spn-103555","text":", or "},{"id":"spn-103556","marks":["italic"],"text":"what happened and why"},{"id":"spn-103557","text":"."}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-72371","spans":[{"id":"spn-103558","text":""}]},{"id":"blk-72372","spans":[{"id":"spn-103559","text":"CrewAI"}]},{"id":"blk-72373","spans":[{"id":"spn-103560","text":"LangGraph"}]},{"id":"blk-72374","spans":[{"id":"spn-103561","text":"AutoGen/SK"}]},{"id":"blk-72375","spans":[{"id":"spn-103562","text":"OpenSentience (OS-006)"}]}],"id":"blk-72370","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-72376","spans":[{"id":"spn-103563","text":"Permission model"}]},{"id":"blk-72377","spans":[{"id":"spn-103564","text":"None"}]},{"id":"blk-72378","spans":[{"id":"spn-103565","text":"None"}]},{"id":"blk-72379","spans":[{"id":"spn-103566","text":"None"}]},{"id":"blk-72380","spans":[{"id":"spn-103567","marks":["bold"],"text":"Deny-by-default policy taxonomy (filesystem, network, tool, graph)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-72381","spans":[{"id":"spn-103568","text":"Audit trail"}]},{"id":"blk-72382","spans":[{"id":"spn-103569","text":"None"}]},{"id":"blk-72383","spans":[{"id":"spn-103570","text":"None"}]},{"id":"blk-72384","spans":[{"id":"spn-103571","text":"None"}]},{"id":"blk-72385","spans":[{"id":"spn-103572","marks":["bold"],"text":"Append-only, immutable, async-batched"}]}],[{"id":"blk-72386","spans":[{"id":"spn-103573","text":"Lifecycle management"}]},{"id":"blk-72387","spans":[{"id":"spn-103574","text":"Binary (running/stopped)"}]},{"id":"blk-72388","spans":[{"id":"spn-103575","text":"Binary"}]},{"id":"blk-72389","spans":[{"id":"spn-103576","text":"Binary"}]},{"id":"blk-72390","spans":[{"id":"spn-103577","marks":["bold"],"text":"4-state (installed, enabled, running, disabled)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-72391","spans":[{"id":"spn-103578","text":"Autonomy levels"}]},{"id":"blk-72392","spans":[{"id":"spn-103579","text":"Binary (full auto or full manual)"}]},{"id":"blk-72393","spans":[{"id":"spn-103580","text":"Binary"}]},{"id":"blk-72394","spans":[{"id":"spn-103581","text":"Binary"}]},{"id":"blk-72395","spans":[{"id":"spn-103582","marks":["bold"],"text":"Graduated (observe, advise, act)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-72396","spans":[{"id":"spn-103583","text":"Governance primitives"}]},{"id":"blk-72397","spans":[{"id":"spn-103584","text":"0"}]},{"id":"blk-72398","spans":[{"id":"spn-103585","text":"0"}]},{"id":"blk-72399","spans":[{"id":"spn-103586","text":"0"}]},{"id":"blk-72400","spans":[{"id":"spn-103587","marks":["bold"],"text":"Policy inheritance, monotonic boundaries, revocable delegation"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-72401","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103588","text":"The gap is not incidental — it is structural. As the OpenSentience spec states: orchestration frameworks assume a single developer controls everything. That assumption breaks at enterprise scale, where you need to know which agent made which decision, under what policy, with what authority, and whether that authority can be revoked."}]},{"id":"blk-72402","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103589","marks":["bold"],"text":"Structural constraint:"},{"id":"spn-103590","text":" Adding governance to an orchestration framework after the fact means adding it as middleware — a permission-check layer that wraps every function call. Middleware governance can always be bypassed: a direct function call, an unregistered tool, a subprocess that skips the wrapper. Governance has to be structural — baked into the supervision tree, the lifecycle state machine, the permission lookup path. Retrofitting it requires an architecture rewrite, not a feature addition."}]},{"id":"blk-72403","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-103591","text":"Category 2: Guardrail systems (input/output filtering)"}]},{"id":"blk-72404","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103592","marks":["bold"],"text":"Competitors:"},{"id":"spn-103593","text":" Guardrails AI, NVIDIA NeMo Guardrails, Lakera Guard"}]},{"id":"blk-72405","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103594","text":"These systems filter what goes into and out of LLM calls. They are validators, not governance primitives."}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-72407","spans":[{"id":"spn-103595","text":""}]},{"id":"blk-72408","spans":[{"id":"spn-103596","text":"Guardrails AI"}]},{"id":"blk-72409","spans":[{"id":"spn-103597","text":"NeMo Guardrails"}]},{"id":"blk-72410","spans":[{"id":"spn-103598","text":"Lakera Guard"}]},{"id":"blk-72411","spans":[{"id":"spn-103599","text":"OpenSentience (OS-006 + OS-008)"}]}],"id":"blk-72406","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-72412","spans":[{"id":"spn-103600","text":"Scope"}]},{"id":"blk-72413","spans":[{"id":"spn-103601","text":"Input/output validation"}]},{"id":"blk-72414","spans":[{"id":"spn-103602","text":"Conversational rails"}]},{"id":"blk-72415","spans":[{"id":"spn-103603","text":"Prompt injection detection"}]},{"id":"blk-72416","spans":[{"id":"spn-103604","marks":["bold"],"text":"Full agent lifecycle governance"}]}],[{"id":"blk-72417","spans":[{"id":"spn-103605","text":"State"}]},{"id":"blk-72418","spans":[{"id":"spn-103606","text":"Stateless (per-call)"}]},{"id":"blk-72419","spans":[{"id":"spn-103607","text":"Stateless (per-call)"}]},{"id":"blk-72420","spans":[{"id":"spn-103608","text":"Stateless (per-call)"}]},{"id":"blk-72421","spans":[{"id":"spn-103609","marks":["bold"],"text":"Stateful (lifecycle, permissions, audit trail persist)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-72422","spans":[{"id":"spn-103610","text":"Pipeline enforcement"}]},{"id":"blk-72423","spans":[{"id":"spn-103611","text":"No"}]},{"id":"blk-72424","spans":[{"id":"spn-103612","text":"No"}]},{"id":"blk-72425","spans":[{"id":"spn-103613","text":"No"}]},{"id":"blk-72426","spans":[{"id":"spn-103614","marks":["bold"],"text":"Yes (OS-008 harness: ordered stages, quality gates)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-72427","spans":[{"id":"spn-103615","text":"Permission model"}]},{"id":"blk-72428","spans":[{"id":"spn-103616","text":"No"}]},{"id":"blk-72429","spans":[{"id":"spn-103617","text":"No"}]},{"id":"blk-72430","spans":[{"id":"spn-103618","text":"No"}]},{"id":"blk-72431","spans":[{"id":"spn-103619","marks":["bold"],"text":"Yes (deny-by-default, taxonomy-based)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-72432","spans":[{"id":"spn-103620","text":"Autonomy graduation"}]},{"id":"blk-72433","spans":[{"id":"spn-103621","text":"No"}]},{"id":"blk-72434","spans":[{"id":"spn-103622","text":"No"}]},{"id":"blk-72435","spans":[{"id":"spn-103623","text":"No"}]},{"id":"blk-72436","spans":[{"id":"spn-103624","marks":["bold"],"text":"Yes (observe/advise/act)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-72437","spans":[{"id":"spn-103625","text":"Agent lifecycle"}]},{"id":"blk-72438","spans":[{"id":"spn-103626","text":"No"}]},{"id":"blk-72439","spans":[{"id":"spn-103627","text":"No"}]},{"id":"blk-72440","spans":[{"id":"spn-103628","text":"No"}]},{"id":"blk-72441","spans":[{"id":"spn-103629","marks":["bold"],"text":"Yes (install/enable/run/disable transitions)"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-72442","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103630","text":"Guardrails check each call independently. They have no memory of previous calls, no concept of agent lifecycle state, and no ability to enforce pipeline ordering. A guardrail cannot say \"this agent is in observe mode and must not execute tool calls\" — it can only say \"this specific output looks unsafe.\""}]},{"id":"blk-72443","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103631","text":"The distinction matters because governance is not content filtering. Governance is: "},{"id":"spn-103632","marks":["italic"],"text":"does this agent have the authority to perform this action, in this lifecycle state, at this autonomy level, and is there an immutable record of the decision?"}]},{"id":"blk-72444","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103633","marks":["bold"],"text":"Structural constraint:"},{"id":"spn-103634","text":" Guardrails are stateless by design. Their API contract is input-in, validated-output-out. Adding lifecycle state, permission persistence, and pipeline ordering transforms them from a validation library into a runtime — a fundamentally different product with a fundamentally different architecture. Every existing integration assumes stateless per-call semantics."}]},{"id":"blk-72445","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-103635","text":"Category 3: Safety and alignment research (theoretical)"}]},{"id":"blk-72446","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103636","marks":["bold"],"text":"Competitors:"},{"id":"spn-103637","text":" Anthropic Constitutional AI, OpenAI safety frameworks, academic alignment research"}]},{"id":"blk-72447","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103638","text":"These organizations publish theoretical principles for AI safety. None of them publish runtime enforcement primitives."}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-72449","spans":[{"id":"spn-103639","text":""}]},{"id":"blk-72450","spans":[{"id":"spn-103640","text":"Anthropic (Constitutional AI)"}]},{"id":"blk-72451","spans":[{"id":"spn-103641","text":"OpenAI (safety frameworks)"}]},{"id":"blk-72452","spans":[{"id":"spn-103642","text":"OpenSentience"}]}],"id":"blk-72448","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-72453","spans":[{"id":"spn-103643","text":"Output"}]},{"id":"blk-72454","spans":[{"id":"spn-103644","text":"Research papers, internal guardrails"}]},{"id":"blk-72455","spans":[{"id":"spn-103645","text":"Internal safety processes"}]},{"id":"blk-72456","spans":[{"id":"spn-103646","marks":["bold"],"text":"Numbered protocols (OS-001 through OS-010) with formal specs"}]}],[{"id":"blk-72457","spans":[{"id":"spn-103647","text":"Runtime enforcement"}]},{"id":"blk-72458","spans":[{"id":"spn-103648","text":"Internal to Claude"}]},{"id":"blk-72459","spans":[{"id":"spn-103649","text":"Internal to GPT"}]},{"id":"blk-72460","spans":[{"id":"spn-103650","marks":["bold"],"text":"Open hex package (`open_sentience`) anyone can deploy"}]}],[{"id":"blk-72461","spans":[{"id":"spn-103651","text":"Cognitive grounding"}]},{"id":"blk-72462","spans":[{"id":"spn-103652","text":"Constitutional principles (normative)"}]},{"id":"blk-72463","spans":[{"id":"spn-103653","text":"RLHF alignment (training-time)"}]},{"id":"blk-72464","spans":[{"id":"spn-103654","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive science mapping (each protocol to established theory)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-72465","spans":[{"id":"spn-103655","text":"External adoption"}]},{"id":"blk-72466","spans":[{"id":"spn-103656","text":"Not a protocol"}]},{"id":"blk-72467","spans":[{"id":"spn-103657","text":"Not a protocol"}]},{"id":"blk-72468","spans":[{"id":"spn-103658","marks":["bold"],"text":"Apache 2.0, spec-driven, third-party implementable"}]}],[{"id":"blk-72469","spans":[{"id":"spn-103659","text":"Harness research"}]},{"id":"blk-72470","spans":[{"id":"spn-103660","text":"Anthropic's 2026 harness work confirms need for external orchestration"}]},{"id":"blk-72471","spans":[{"id":"spn-103661","text":"—"}]},{"id":"blk-72472","spans":[{"id":"spn-103662","marks":["bold"],"text":"OS-008 ships the harness as a deployable artifact"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-72473","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103663","text":"Anthropic's 2026 research into agent harnesses validates the core thesis: models need external orchestration to be safe. But research organizations publish findings, not protocols. The gap between \"we proved agents need harnesses\" and \"here is a deployable harness with pipeline enforcement, quality gates, and sprint contracts\" is the gap OpenSentience fills."}]},{"id":"blk-72474","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103664","marks":["bold"],"text":"Structural constraint:"},{"id":"spn-103665","text":" Research organizations are not protocol publishers. Their incentive is to advance the field, not to ship interoperable specs with version numbers, schema definitions, and reference implementations. Converting research findings into adoptable standards requires a different organizational structure — one optimized for protocol design and ecosystem adoption rather than paper publication."}]},{"id":"blk-72475","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-103666","text":"Category 4: Cloud platform governance (lock-in)"}]},{"id":"blk-72476","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103667","marks":["bold"],"text":"Competitors:"},{"id":"spn-103668","text":" AWS Bedrock Guardrails, Azure AI Safety, Google Vertex AI Safety"}]},{"id":"blk-72477","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103669","text":"These platforms offer governance features tied to their cloud. The governance is real — and non-portable."}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-72479","spans":[{"id":"spn-103670","text":""}]},{"id":"blk-72480","spans":[{"id":"spn-103671","text":"AWS Bedrock"}]},{"id":"blk-72481","spans":[{"id":"spn-103672","text":"Azure AI Safety"}]},{"id":"blk-72482","spans":[{"id":"spn-103673","text":"Google Vertex AI"}]},{"id":"blk-72483","spans":[{"id":"spn-103674","text":"OpenSentience"}]}],"id":"blk-72478","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-72484","spans":[{"id":"spn-103675","text":"Governance quality"}]},{"id":"blk-72485","spans":[{"id":"spn-103676","text":"Good (within AWS)"}]},{"id":"blk-72486","spans":[{"id":"spn-103677","text":"Good (within Azure)"}]},{"id":"blk-72487","spans":[{"id":"spn-103678","text":"Good (within GCP)"}]},{"id":"blk-72488","spans":[{"id":"spn-103679","marks":["bold"],"text":"Good (anywhere)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-72489","spans":[{"id":"spn-103680","text":"Portability"}]},{"id":"blk-72490","spans":[{"id":"spn-103681","text":"None"}]},{"id":"blk-72491","spans":[{"id":"spn-103682","text":"None"}]},{"id":"blk-72492","spans":[{"id":"spn-103683","text":"None"}]},{"id":"blk-72493","spans":[{"id":"spn-103684","marks":["bold"],"text":"Full (Apache 2.0, OTP-native)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-72494","spans":[{"id":"spn-103685","text":"Edge deployment"}]},{"id":"blk-72495","spans":[{"id":"spn-103686","text":"No (cloud-only)"}]},{"id":"blk-72496","spans":[{"id":"spn-103687","text":"No (cloud-only)"}]},{"id":"blk-72497","spans":[{"id":"spn-103688","text":"No (cloud-only)"}]},{"id":"blk-72498","spans":[{"id":"spn-103689","marks":["bold"],"text":"Yes (ETS-based, no external deps)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-72499","spans":[{"id":"spn-103690","text":"Multi-cloud"}]},{"id":"blk-72500","spans":[{"id":"spn-103691","text":"No"}]},{"id":"blk-72501","spans":[{"id":"spn-103692","text":"No"}]},{"id":"blk-72502","spans":[{"id":"spn-103693","text":"No"}]},{"id":"blk-72503","spans":[{"id":"spn-103694","marks":["bold"],"text":"Yes (runs on any BEAM host)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-72504","spans":[{"id":"spn-103695","text":"Vendor lock-in"}]},{"id":"blk-72505","spans":[{"id":"spn-103696","text":"By design"}]},{"id":"blk-72506","spans":[{"id":"spn-103697","text":"By design"}]},{"id":"blk-72507","spans":[{"id":"spn-103698","text":"By design"}]},{"id":"blk-72508","spans":[{"id":"spn-103699","marks":["bold"],"text":"None"}]}],[{"id":"blk-72509","spans":[{"id":"spn-103700","text":"Permission latency"}]},{"id":"blk-72510","spans":[{"id":"spn-103701","text":"Network round-trip"}]},{"id":"blk-72511","spans":[{"id":"spn-103702","text":"Network round-trip"}]},{"id":"blk-72512","spans":[{"id":"spn-103703","text":"Network round-trip"}]},{"id":"blk-72513","spans":[{"id":"spn-103704","marks":["bold"],"text":"< 2 microseconds (ETS lookup)"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-72514","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103705","text":"The competitive dynamic here is financial, not technical. These platforms "},{"id":"spn-103706","marks":["italic"],"text":"can"},{"id":"spn-103707","text":" build portable governance. Their revenue model will not allow it. An enterprise customer's governance policies being portable to a competitor's cloud is an existential threat to platform retention metrics."}]},{"id":"blk-72515","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103708","text":"AWS Bedrock Guardrails are good guardrails — for workloads that will never leave AWS. The moment an organization runs agents across clouds, at the edge, or on-premise, cloud-scoped governance becomes a constraint rather than a feature."}]},{"id":"blk-72516","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103709","marks":["bold"],"text":"Structural constraint:"},{"id":"spn-103710","text":" Portability is an existential threat to cloud platform business models. These companies have optimized for ecosystem retention. Opening the governance layer means enabling customers to leave. Their architecture and their revenue model are aligned around preventing exactly the portability that OpenSentience provides."}]},{"id":"blk-72517","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-103711","text":"Category 5: Multi-agent consensus"}]},{"id":"blk-72518","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103712","marks":["bold"],"text":"Competitors:"},{"id":"spn-103713","text":" None (effectively)."}]},{"id":"blk-72519","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103714","text":"Google A2A solves agent-to-agent discovery and delegation. It does not solve consensus, durable state, or governance."}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-72521","spans":[{"id":"spn-103715","text":""}]},{"id":"blk-72522","spans":[{"id":"spn-103716","text":"Google A2A"}]},{"id":"blk-72523","spans":[{"id":"spn-103717","text":"IBM ACP"}]},{"id":"blk-72524","spans":[{"id":"spn-103718","text":"AgenTroMatic + Delegatic (via OpenSentience protocols)"}]}],"id":"blk-72520","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-72525","spans":[{"id":"spn-103719","text":"Multi-party consensus"}]},{"id":"blk-72526","spans":[{"id":"spn-103720","text":"No"}]},{"id":"blk-72527","spans":[{"id":"spn-103721","text":"No"}]},{"id":"blk-72528","spans":[{"id":"spn-103722","marks":["bold"],"text":"Yes (quorum validation, Raft-based)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-72529","spans":[{"id":"spn-103723","text":"Durable deliberation state"}]},{"id":"blk-72530","spans":[{"id":"spn-103724","text":"No (ephemeral)"}]},{"id":"blk-72531","spans":[{"id":"spn-103725","text":"No"}]},{"id":"blk-72532","spans":[{"id":"spn-103726","marks":["bold"],"text":"Yes (persistent context across rounds)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-72533","spans":[{"id":"spn-103727","text":"Governance integration"}]},{"id":"blk-72534","spans":[{"id":"spn-103728","text":"No"}]},{"id":"blk-72535","spans":[{"id":"spn-103729","text":"No"}]},{"id":"blk-72536","spans":[{"id":"spn-103730","marks":["bold"],"text":"Yes (OS-006 policy inheritance, monotonic boundaries)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-72537","spans":[{"id":"spn-103731","text":"Topology-derived routing"}]},{"id":"blk-72538","spans":[{"id":"spn-103732","text":"No"}]},{"id":"blk-72539","spans":[{"id":"spn-103733","text":"No"}]},{"id":"blk-72540","spans":[{"id":"spn-103734","marks":["bold"],"text":"Yes (kappa-routing decides deliberation rights)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-72541","spans":[{"id":"spn-103735","text":"Autonomy levels"}]},{"id":"blk-72542","spans":[{"id":"spn-103736","text":"No"}]},{"id":"blk-72543","spans":[{"id":"spn-103737","text":"No"}]},{"id":"blk-72544","spans":[{"id":"spn-103738","marks":["bold"],"text":"Yes (observe/advise/act per agent per context)"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-72545","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103739","text":"A2A is a transport protocol. It answers \"how do agents talk to each other?\" It does not answer \"how do agents reach agreement?\", \"who has the authority to make this decision?\", or \"what happens when agents disagree?\" These are governance questions, and A2A explicitly leaves them out of scope."}]},{"id":"blk-72546","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103740","text":"The AgenTroMatic and Delegatic specs — both grounded in OpenSentience protocols OS-003 and OS-006 — fill exactly this gap. They build consensus and governance "},{"id":"spn-103741","marks":["italic"],"text":"on top of"},{"id":"spn-103742","text":" A2A, not in competition with it."}]},{"id":"blk-72547","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103743","marks":["bold"],"text":"Structural constraint:"},{"id":"spn-103744","text":" A2A is now in the Linux Foundation's Agentic AI Foundation. Adding consensus, governance, and durable state requires revising a spec in committee. That process takes years. The deliberation and governance layers can be built on top of A2A today — the [&] portfolio does exactly this — while the committee process catches up."}]},{"id":"blk-72548","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-103745","text":"OpenSentience differentiators"}]},{"id":"blk-72549","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103746","text":"Nine structural advantages that no competitor combines:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-72551","spans":[{"id":"spn-103747","text":"#"}]},{"id":"blk-72552","spans":[{"id":"spn-103748","text":"Differentiator"}]},{"id":"blk-72553","spans":[{"id":"spn-103749","text":"Detail"}]}],"id":"blk-72550","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-72554","spans":[{"id":"spn-103750","text":"1"}]},{"id":"blk-72555","spans":[{"id":"spn-103751","marks":["bold"],"text":"Protocol-first"}]},{"id":"blk-72556","spans":[{"id":"spn-103752","text":"Numbered specs (OS-001 through OS-010) with formal definitions, not just code"}]}],[{"id":"blk-72557","spans":[{"id":"spn-103753","text":"2"}]},{"id":"blk-72558","spans":[{"id":"spn-103754","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive science grounding"}]},{"id":"blk-72559","spans":[{"id":"spn-103755","text":"Each protocol maps to established cognitive science — continual learning to memory consolidation, attention to executive function, deliberation to dual-process theory"}]}],[{"id":"blk-72560","spans":[{"id":"spn-103756","text":"3"}]},{"id":"blk-72561","spans":[{"id":"spn-103757","marks":["bold"],"text":"Graduated autonomy"}]},{"id":"blk-72562","spans":[{"id":"spn-103758","text":"Three levels (observe, advise, act) — no other system provides runtime-adjustable autonomy with audit trails for each transition"}]}],[{"id":"blk-72563","spans":[{"id":"spn-103759","text":"4"}]},{"id":"blk-72564","spans":[{"id":"spn-103760","marks":["bold"],"text":"Topology-derived governance"}]},{"id":"blk-72565","spans":[{"id":"spn-103761","text":"kappa-routing (OS-002) decides deliberation rights — governance emerges from graph structure, not from configuration files"}]}],[{"id":"blk-72566","spans":[{"id":"spn-103762","text":"5"}]},{"id":"blk-72567","spans":[{"id":"spn-103763","marks":["bold"],"text":"Thin shim architecture"}]},{"id":"blk-72568","spans":[{"id":"spn-103764","text":"< 1% overhead, < 2 microsecond permission checks via ETS — governance that costs nothing at runtime"}]}],[{"id":"blk-72569","spans":[{"id":"spn-103765","text":"6"}]},{"id":"blk-72570","spans":[{"id":"spn-103766","marks":["bold"],"text":"Harness enforcement (OS-008)"}]},{"id":"blk-72571","spans":[{"id":"spn-103767","text":"Pipeline ordering, quality gates, sprint contracts, context management — the deployable artifact that Anthropic's research says is necessary"}]}],[{"id":"blk-72572","spans":[{"id":"spn-103768","text":"7"}]},{"id":"blk-72573","spans":[{"id":"spn-103769","marks":["bold"],"text":"Diagnostic algebra (OS-009 PRISM)"}]},{"id":"blk-72574","spans":[{"id":"spn-103770","text":"9 continual-learning dimensions, BYOR ingestion, IRT calibration, leaderboards — measures whether a closed memory loop actually learns over time, not just whether it answers questions"}]}],[{"id":"blk-72575","spans":[{"id":"spn-103771","text":"8"}]},{"id":"blk-72576","spans":[{"id":"spn-103772","marks":["bold"],"text":"Temporal algebra (OS-010 PULSE)"}]},{"id":"blk-72577","spans":[{"id":"spn-103773","text":"Loop manifest standard with 5 canonical phase kinds, 5 cross-loop tokens (CloudEvents v1), 7 invariants, and a 12-test conformance suite — turns inter-system integration from ad-hoc to algebraic"}]}],[{"id":"blk-72578","spans":[{"id":"spn-103774","text":"9"}]},{"id":"blk-72579","spans":[{"id":"spn-103775","marks":["bold"],"text":"Open (Apache 2.0)"}]},{"id":"blk-72580","spans":[{"id":"spn-103776","text":"Every protocol, every spec, every reference implementation — no lock-in, no proprietary layer"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-72581","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-103777","text":"The commoditization argument"}]},{"id":"blk-72582","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103778","text":"As AI-generated code approaches commodity (2026-2030):"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-72584","spans":[{"id":"spn-103779","text":"What loses value"}]},{"id":"blk-72585","spans":[{"id":"spn-103780","text":"Why"}]},{"id":"blk-72586","spans":[{"id":"spn-103781","text":"What gains value"}]},{"id":"blk-72587","spans":[{"id":"spn-103782","text":"Why"}]}],"id":"blk-72583","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-72588","spans":[{"id":"spn-103783","text":"Guardrail implementations"}]},{"id":"blk-72589","spans":[{"id":"spn-103784","text":"Any LLM can generate input/output filters"}]},{"id":"blk-72590","spans":[{"id":"spn-103785","marks":["bold"],"text":"Governance protocols"}]},{"id":"blk-72591","spans":[{"id":"spn-103786","text":"Policy inheritance and audit immutability require adoption, not generation"}]}],[{"id":"blk-72592","spans":[{"id":"spn-103787","text":"Agent frameworks"}]},{"id":"blk-72593","spans":[{"id":"spn-103788","text":"Any LLM can scaffold agent wiring"}]},{"id":"blk-72594","spans":[{"id":"spn-103789","marks":["bold"],"text":"Lifecycle enforcement primitives"}]},{"id":"blk-72595","spans":[{"id":"spn-103790","text":"State machines with deny-by-default semantics are architectural commitments"}]}],[{"id":"blk-72596","spans":[{"id":"spn-103791","text":"Platform safety features"}]},{"id":"blk-72597","spans":[{"id":"spn-103792","text":"Any LLM can replicate feature sets"}]},{"id":"blk-72598","spans":[{"id":"spn-103793","marks":["bold"],"text":"Portable governance specs"}]},{"id":"blk-72599","spans":[{"id":"spn-103794","text":"Numbered protocols with reference implementations create ecosystem gravity"}]}],[{"id":"blk-72600","spans":[{"id":"spn-103795","text":"Alignment research papers"}]},{"id":"blk-72601","spans":[{"id":"spn-103796","text":"Findings are public knowledge"}]},{"id":"blk-72602","spans":[{"id":"spn-103797","marks":["bold"],"text":"Deployable harness artifacts"}]},{"id":"blk-72603","spans":[{"id":"spn-103798","text":"The gap between research and runtime is the gap that accrues value"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-72604","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103799","text":"Every competitor in categories 1-4 sells "},{"id":"spn-103800","marks":["italic"],"text":"implementation"},{"id":"spn-103801","text":". Implementation is the thing that gets commoditized. OpenSentience sells "},{"id":"spn-103802","marks":["italic"],"text":"protocols, cognitive grounding, and enforcement primitives"},{"id":"spn-103803","text":" — the things that survive commoditization."}]},{"id":"blk-72605","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-103804","text":"The thesis"}]},{"id":"blk-72606","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103805","text":"Every competitor in the agent governance space has optimized for a local maximum:"}]},{"id":"blk-72607","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-72609","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103806","marks":["bold"],"text":"Orchestration frameworks"},{"id":"spn-103807","text":" optimized for developer simplicity — cannot add governance without middleware that can be bypassed"}]}],"id":"blk-72608","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-72611","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103808","marks":["bold"],"text":"Guardrail systems"},{"id":"spn-103809","text":" optimized for stateless per-call validation — cannot add lifecycle state without becoming a different product"}]}],"id":"blk-72610","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-72613","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103810","marks":["bold"],"text":"Safety researchers"},{"id":"spn-103811","text":" optimized for theoretical rigor — cannot ship adoptable protocols without becoming a standards organization"}]}],"id":"blk-72612","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-72615","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103812","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cloud platforms"},{"id":"spn-103813","text":" optimized for ecosystem lock-in — cannot open governance without threatening their retention revenue"}]}],"id":"blk-72614","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-72617","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103814","marks":["bold"],"text":"Protocol committees"},{"id":"spn-103815","text":" optimized for consensus — cannot move fast enough to fill their own composition gaps"}]}],"id":"blk-72616","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-72618","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103816","text":"OpenSentience occupies the structural position none of them can reach: an open governance layer with cognitive science grounding, graduated autonomy, topology-derived enforcement, and a protocol-series architecture where each numbered spec makes the others more valuable."}]},{"id":"blk-72619","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103817","text":"As code generation commoditizes implementation, the value migrates to governance protocols, cognitive primitives, and enforcement standards. OpenSentience defines all three."}]},{"id":"blk-72620","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103818","marks":["italic"],"text":"OpenSentience -- opensentience.org -- Apache 2.0"}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaierawkljib6rlv73ycqdhtiuo46s77t6ea6ei4pbmhprnm2qn4decvaq","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}